From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:07:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] model : add Ricursive (ricursiveAI Ripple-65B-Preview)

New architecture `ricursive` (HF RicursiveForCausalLM, custom code). A dense
decoder assembled from pieces llama.cpp already has plus one small addition:

- PeriNorm blocks: RMSNorm before and after both attention and the FFN
  (attn_norm, post_attention_norm, ffn_norm, post_ffw_norm), per-head Q/K
  RMSNorm applied before RoPE, untied lm_head.
- Hybrid attention: four sliding-window layers (RoPE, window 1024) then one
  full-attention layer with no positional encoding. Stored as
  attention.sliding_window + sliding_window_pattern, graph ropes only
  is_swa(il) layers. Period 5 is the default when the pattern is absent.
- Gated attention: attention output * sigmoid(g_proj(normed input)) before
  o_proj. g_proj rides the existing attn_gate tensor.
- Value residual: the V projection reads lerp(layer-0 embeddings, x,
  sigmoid(lambda)) with one learned scalar per layer. The converter folds the
  per-layer value_res_lambda tensors into a float array
  `ricursive.attention.value_residual_lambda`; the graph applies the blend as
  two scales and an add (no extra tensors).
- Clamped SwiGLU: silu(min(gate, c)) * clamp(up, -c, c) via the existing
  ggml_swiglu_clamp, c stored as `ricursive.swiglu_clamp` (0 = plain SwiGLU).
- Embedding scale from `embed_scale` (sqrt(n_embd) on the non-folded
  checkpoint) through the existing embedding_scale key; build_inp_embd
  applies it.

Converter: conversion/ricursive.py registered for RicursiveForCausalLM, gpt2
vocab (the tokenizer hashes to the dbrx pre-tokenizer, 100278 real tokens
padded to the 100352 embedding rows), ChatML chat template from
tokenizer_config.

Validated on a tiny random checkpoint against an independent PyTorch
implementation of the block written from the published modeling code:
per-token final hidden states cosine >= 0.99998 and top-10 next-token ids
identical (<= 0.4% relative probability error) on CUDA with flash attention
on and off, on CPU, and with the prompt split across micro-batches of 16 and
7 tokens so the SWA cache path is exercised.
